  "answer": "Project Zenith is a new initiative aimed at revolutionizing data analytics, with a kick-off on June 15th and a Phase One budget of $500,000, led by Sarah Tan. The project involves gathering innovative ideas by July 20th to leverage AI in data visualization. Initial findings suggest a potential 20% efficiency increase, to be discussed on August 5th. The team expanded to include five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, with an onboarding session on September 10th. Additional team members Mike Chen (machine learning) and Lisa Ray (cloud computing) were also welcomed. Following the design phase, the development phase began next month, led by Omar Jensen. A major milestone was reached ahead of schedule with the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype, and user interface enhancements are planned for October. Feedback on the prototype's performance and user experience is being sought by the end of November. The project is now nearing its final stages."
